{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bh88a81jp","tool_use_id":"toolu_01K9Vbi3aW9pZ4Db6wKvyrMa","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run3-repo/f353c22b-f36d-4bec-831b-66c75635cc53/tasks/bh88a81jp.output","summary":"Background command \"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop\npython3 - <<'PY'\nsrc=open(\"models/second_order_chance_motif_suspicion.py\").read()\nd=\"iter_3/candidate_3/\"\nreps=[('''\"\"\"Second-order chance coin in the person-specific motif-suspicion judgment.\n''','''\"\"\"Face-biased, second-order chance coin in the person-specific motif-suspicion judgment.\n\nRefinement of the incumbent `second_order_chance_motif_suspicion`. Single change\n(a component grafted from `chance_face_bias_motif_suspicion`): the person's\nsecond-order model of a fair coin is also not label-symmetric -- it believes heads\ncome up with probability theta (shared, fitted), so the chance log-likelihood\ndifference of a pair gains (h_a - h_b) * logit(theta), weighed by the person's\nsensitivity like the rest of the evidence; tail-leaning sequences look more random\nif theta < 0.5. Addresses the FDR-surviving critique that people choose the\nhead-heavier sequence less often than the H/T-symmetric incumbent predicts.\n\nOriginal description of the incumbent follows.\n'''),\n('out = {\"k\": float(k),','out = {\"h\": float(h), \"k\": float(k),'),\n('idx_a, idx_b, switch_diff, alt2_diff, pid, y = [], [], [], [], [], []','idx_a, idx_b, switch_diff, alt2_diff, heads_diff, pid, y = [], [], [], [], [], [], []'),\n('''        alt2_diff.append(table[ia_ib[0]][\"alt2\"] - table[ia_ib[1]][\"alt2\"])\n''','''        alt2_diff.append(table[ia_ib[0]][\"alt2\"] - table[ia_ib[1]][\"alt2\"])\n        heads_diff.append(table[ia_ib[0]][\"h\"] - table[ia_ib[1]][\"h\"])\n'''),\n('''        \"alt2_diff\": np.asarray(alt2_diff, dtype=\"float64\"),\n''','''        \"alt2_diff\": np.asarray(alt2_diff, dtype=\"float64\"),\n        \"heads_diff\": np.asarray(heads_diff, dtype=\"float64\"),\n'''),\n('''    alt2_diff = pm.Data(\"alt2_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n''','''    alt2_diff = pm.Data(\"alt2_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    heads_diff = pm.Data(\"heads_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n'''),\n('''    pid = participant_id\n    log_chance2_diff = 0.5 * d_switch2 * alt2_diff\n''','''    # Believed heads probability of a fair coin, as its logit (0: symmetric).\n    logit_theta = pm.Normal(\"logit_theta\", mu=0.0, sigma=0.5)\n\n    pid = participant_id\n    log_chance2_diff = 0.5 * d_switch2 * alt2_diff + logit_theta * heads_diff\n''')]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    assert src.count(a)==1, a\n    src=src.replace(a,b)\nopen(d+\"candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_3 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5; ls /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_3\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"e17a2d67-e425-43b7-b0bb-27bb37f93703","session_id":"f353c22b-f36d-4bec-831b-66c75635cc53"}
